[ti:Amazing Grace]
[au:John Newton, 1779 (public domain)]
[00:02.66]Amazing grace! How sweet the sound
[00:15.40]That saved a wretch like me!
[00:24.09]I once was lost, but now am found;
[00:35.64]Was blind, but now I see.
[00:46.90]'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear,
[00:57.23]And grace my fears relieved;
[01:08.47]How precious did that grace appear
[01:18.29]The hour I first believed.
[01:28.03]Through many dangers, toils and snares,
[01:38.16]I have already come;
[01:48.75]'Tis grace hath brought me safe thus far,
[01:59.05]And grace will lead me home.
The Lord has promised good to me,
His word my hope secures;
He will my shield and portion be,
As long as life endures.
Yea, when this flesh and heart shall fail,
And mortal life shall cease,
I shall possess, within the veil,
A life of joy and peace.
When we've been there ten thousand years,
Bright shining as the sun,
We've no less days to sing God's praise
Than when we'd first begun.
